-- title:
--   Residue of a dx pulled back to the upper half-plane
-- statement:
--   Fix $N\ge 1$ and write $F=$ [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange ℂ (ModularCurve.modularFunctionFieldFull N)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the subfield of $\mathbb C((q))$ generated over $\mathbb C$ by the coefficientwise images of the field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the $q$-expansions $q\mathrm{Expand}_{\mathbb Q}\,d\,j_q$ for divisors $d\mid N$. Let $D$ be a [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary N`](def/ModularCurve_ComplexPlaceDictionary.html#L28): a map $\tau\mapsto P_\tau$ from $\mathfrak H$ to places of $F/\mathbb C$ together with positive integers $e_\tau$, invariant under $\Gamma_0(N)$, such that $y$ lies in the valuation subring of $P_\tau$ exactly when $\tau\mapsto\lVert\mathrm{realize}\,N\,y\rVert$ is bounded near $\tau$ on the punctured neighbourhood filter, and such that the meromorphic order at $\tau$ of $z\mapsto \mathrm{realize}\,N\,y(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)$ equals $e_\tau\cdot\operatorname{ord}_{P_\tau}(y)$ for $y\neq0$; here $\mathrm{realize}\,N\,y\,\tau$ is defined by choosing modular forms $g,h$ of some common weight on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with $h(\tau)\neq0$ and $y\cdot q\text{-exp}(h)=q\text{-exp}(g)$, and returning $g(\tau)/h(\tau)$ (and $0$ if no such choice exists). Assume every place $w$ of $F/\mathbb C$ satisfies `DCoordGenerates`, i.e. $w.\mathrm{dCoord}=d\pi_w$ for the chosen uniformizer $\pi_w$ spans $\Omega_{F/\mathbb C}$ over $F$. Let $a,x,\pi\in F$, $\tau\in\mathfrak H$ and $\eta\in\Omega_{F/\mathbb C}$, put $v=P_\tau$, and suppose $\eta=a\,dx$, $\eta\neq0$, $\operatorname{ord}_v(c)\ge-1$ where $c=v.\mathrm{differentialCoeff}\,\eta$ is the element with $\eta=c\cdot v.\mathrm{dCoord}$, $\operatorname{ord}_v(\pi)=1$, and $v.\mathrm{dCoord}=d\pi$. Then there are $\rho\in\mathbb C$ and $g:\mathbb C\to\mathbb C$ such that $c\pi-\rho$ is a nonunit of the valuation subring of $v$, $\rho\neq0$ if and only if $\operatorname{ord}_v(c)=-1$, $g$ is analytic at $\tau$, and for all $z$ in a punctured neighbourhood of $\tau$ in $\mathbb C$, $$\mathrm{realize}\,N\,a(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)\cdot \frac{d}{dz}\,\mathrm{realize}\,N\,x(\mathrm{ofComplex}\,z)=\frac{e_\tau\,\rho}{z-\tau}+g(z).$$
--
--   This is the comparison between the algebraic residue of a differential $\eta=a\,dx$ of the function field of $X_0(N)$ over $\mathbb C$ at the place below $\tau$ and the analytic Laurent expansion at $\tau$ of the pull-back of $\eta$ to the upper half-plane, the ramification index $e_\tau$ of $\mathfrak H\to Y_0(N)$ appearing as the factor relating $d\pi/\pi$ to $dz/(z-\tau)$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.exists_slashInvariant_residue_ne_zero_of_pt_ne`](thm.html#ModularCurve.ComplexPlaceDictionary.exists_slashInvariant_residue_ne_zero_of_pt_ne), where a differential with prescribed nonvanishing residue at a prescribed point is produced.
